===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*nemaną}}, probably from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*nem-||take}}.

Germanic cognates include {{cog|osx|niman}}, {{cog|odt|neman}} ({{cog|nl|nemen}}), {{cog|goh|neman}} ({{cog|de|nehmen}}), {{cog|non|nema}} ({{cog|da|nemme}}), {{cog|got|𐌽𐌹𐌼𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root was also the source of {{cog|sga|nem||present}}, {{cog|lv|ņemt||to take}}, {{cog|sq|nëm||to take, curse}}, {{cog|grc|νέμω}}.

